{"id":"zip-0257","number":257,"title":"Deployment of the Orchard Temporary Vulnerability Mitigation and NU6.2 Network Upgrade","status":"Final","statusDetail":null,"category":"Consensus / Network","owners":["Daira-Emma Hopwood"],"created":"2026-06-09","license":"MIT","discussionsTo":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/issues/1293","pullRequest":null,"kind":"zip","format":"md","source":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/blob/main/zips/zip-0257.md","official":"https://zips.z.cash/zip-0257","updatedAt":"2026-07-05T07:51:10Z","summary":"This ZIP retrospectively documents the deployment of the Orchard temporary vulnerability mitigation, and the NU6.2 network upgrade.","words":1366,"digest":"40c6dd9cf66d04a464e0e423c2dc06077d5799276c274424acd87ae3352fa79a","headings":[{"id":"terminology","title":"Terminology","level":2},{"id":"abstract","title":"Abstract","level":2},{"id":"motivation","title":"Motivation","level":2},{"id":"specification","title":"Specification","level":2},{"id":"orchardtemporaryvulnerabilitymitigation","title":"Orchard temporary vulnerability mitigation","level":3},{"id":"nu6.2deployment","title":"NU6.2 deployment","level":3},{"id":"zcashprotocolspecificationchanges","title":"Zcash Protocol Specification changes","level":3},{"id":"consensusruleforthetemporaryvulnerabilitymitigation","title":"Consensus rule for the temporary vulnerability mitigation","level":4},{"id":"orchardactionverifyingkeyselection","title":"Orchard Action verifying key selection","level":4},{"id":"canonicalorchardactionprooflength","title":"Canonical Orchard Action proof length","level":4},{"id":"backwardcompatibility","title":"Backward compatibility","level":3},{"id":"references","title":"References","level":2}],"body":[{"tag":"h2","children":["Terminology"],"id":"terminology"},{"tag":"p","children":["The key words “MUST” and “MUST NOT” in this document are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["1"],"id":"fnref1","href":"#fn1"}]}," when, and only when, they appear in all capitals."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The term “network upgrade” in this document is to be interpreted as described in ZIP 200. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["2"],"id":"fnref2","href":"#fn2"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The character § is used when referring to sections of the Zcash Protocol Specification. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["3"],"id":"fnref3","href":"#fn3"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The terms “Mainnet” and “Testnet” are to be interpreted as described in § 3.12 ‘Mainnet and Testnet’. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["4"],"id":"fnref4","href":"#fn4"}]}]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Abstract"],"id":"abstract"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP retrospectively documents the deployment of the Orchard temporary vulnerability mitigation, and the NU6.2 network upgrade."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Motivation"],"id":"motivation"},{"tag":"p","children":["On 2026-05-29, security researcher Taylor Hornby, who had been tasked with an AI-assisted security audit of the Orchard shielded protocol, reported a soundness vulnerability in the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Orchard Action circuit implementation"],"href":"https://github.com/zcash/orchard"},". Details of the vulnerability are described in Taylor’s work log ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["5"],"id":"fnref5","href":"#fn5"}]}," and in GHSA-ww9q-8r59-xv46. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"id":"fnref6","href":"#fn6"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["This vulnerability could have allowed balance violation and theft of funds. Therefore, it was imperative to immediately disable use of Orchard, until a corrected Orchard Action circuit could be deployed in the NU6.2 network upgrade. (Disabling the vulnerable circuit and enabling the new one at the same time was ruled out due to the risk of revealing the vulnerability before it had been mitigated, and in order to close the vulnerability window more quickly, while the fix was still being prepared and reviewed.)"]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Specification"],"id":"specification"},{"tag":"h3","children":["Orchard temporary vulnerability mitigation"],"id":"orchardtemporaryvulnerabilitymitigation"},{"tag":"p","children":["Consensus rule: From block height 3363426 (Mainnet) or 4048500 (Testnet) onward, until the activation of NU6.2 on each network, v5 and later transactions MUST NOT contain any Orchard Action descriptions, i.e. ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖠"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖼"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗌"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖮"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗋"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖼"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗁"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖺"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗋"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖽"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":["="]},{"tag":"mn","children":["0"]}]},"."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Mainnet mitigation was deployed as an emergency hotfix in zcashd v6.12.5 and zebra v4.5.3. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["7"],"id":"fnref7","href":"#fn7"}]}," ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["8"],"id":"fnref8","href":"#fn8"}]}," These releases did not have the “until the activation of NU6.2” restriction; i.e. they disabled Orchard until deployment of the subsequent releases. Note that zcashd v6.12.4 also deployed other security fixes described in ZIP 256 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["9"],"id":"fnref9","href":"#fn9"}]},"."]},{"tag":"p","children":["zcashd v6.12.4 had used a Mainnet activation height of 3363366, 60 blocks earlier. Some mining pools failed to upgrade in time, so the activation was re-attempted successfully at the height given above."]},{"tag":"p","children":["These emergency hotfixes enabled the soft fork on Mainnet only, leaving the Testnet mitigation height unset. On Testnet, the soft fork instead took effect through zcashd v6.20.0 and zebra v5.0.0, which set the Testnet mitigation height to 4048500 and added support for NU6.2. Those releases had been published before Testnet reached height 4048500. The disabling of Orchard, and the subsequent re-enabling at NU6.2 (height 4052000), therefore occurred on Testnet as an ordinary scheduled activation rather than an emergency response."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["NU6.2 deployment"],"id":"nu6.2deployment"},{"tag":"p","children":["The NU6.2 network upgrade re-enables the Orchard shielded protocol, with two consensus changes relative to the original Orchard rules:"]},{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["The Orchard Action circuit’s variable-base scalar multiplication gadget is corrected, fixing the soundness vulnerability. This changes the Orchard verifying key. Pre-NU6.2 Action proofs verify only under the historical (insecure) verifying key, and NU6.2-onward proofs only under the corrected one. The fix was published in halo2_gadgets v0.5.0 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["10"],"id":"fnref10","href":"#fn10"}]}," and orchard v0.14.0. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["11"],"id":"fnref11","href":"#fn11"}]}]}]},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["From the activation of NU6.2, an Orchard Action proof MUST have the canonical length for the corrected circuit. Before NU6.2, this length was not enforced as a consensus rule. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["8"],"id":"fnref8:1","href":"#fn8"}]}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["From the activation of NU6.2, the temporary mitigation no longer applies. Transactions containing Orchard Action descriptions MUST again be accepted, with proofs subject to verification under the corrected circuit and the canonical-length rule. NU6.2 was deployed in zcashd v6.20.0 and zebra v5.0.0."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The primary sources of information about NU6.2 consensus protocol changes are the Zcash Protocol Specification ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["3"],"id":"fnref3:1","href":"#fn3"}]}," and this ZIP."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The network handshake and peer management mechanisms defined in ZIP 201 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["12"],"id":"fnref12","href":"#fn12"}]}," also apply to this upgrade."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The following network upgrade constants ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["2"],"id":"fnref2:1","href":"#fn2"}]}," are defined for the NU6.2 upgrade:"]},{"tag":"dl","children":[{"tag":"dt","children":["CONSENSUS_BRANCH_ID"]},{"tag":"dd","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["0x5437F330"]}]},{"tag":"dt","children":["ACTIVATION_HEIGHT (NU6.2)"]},{"tag":"dd","children":["Testnet: 4052000"]},{"tag":"dd","children":["Mainnet: 3364600"]},{"tag":"dt","children":["MIN_NETWORK_PROTOCOL_VERSION (NU6.2)"]},{"tag":"dd","children":["Testnet: ",{"tag":"code","children":["170150"]}]},{"tag":"dd","children":["Mainnet: ",{"tag":"code","children":["170150"]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["For each network (Testnet and Mainnet), nodes compatible with NU6.2 activation on that network MUST advertise a network protocol version that is greater than or equal to the MIN_NETWORK_PROTOCOL_VERSION (NU6.2) for that activation."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Zcash Protocol Specification changes"],"id":"zcashprotocolspecificationchanges"},{"tag":"p","children":["The changes below to the Zcash Protocol Specification correspond to the two NU6.2 consensus changes described above. They are relative to version 2026.6.4 of the specification ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["13"],"id":"fnref13","href":"#fn13"}]},", and are applied in version 2026.7.0 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["3"],"id":"fnref3:2","href":"#fn3"}]},"."]},{"tag":"h4","children":["Consensus rule for the temporary vulnerability mitigation"],"id":"consensusruleforthetemporaryvulnerabilitymitigation"},{"tag":"p","children":["Add a consensus rule to § 7.1.2 ‘Transaction Consensus Rules’ ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["14"],"id":"fnref14","href":"#fn14"}]},":"]},{"tag":"blockquote","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["[Pre-NU6.2] From block height 3363426 (Mainnet) or 4048500 (Testnet) onward, until the activation of NU6.2 on each network, if ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖿"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖿"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖼"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗏"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖵"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗋"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗌"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":["≥"]},{"tag":"mn","children":["5"]}]}," then the transaction MUST NOT contain any Orchard Action descriptions, i.e. ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖠"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖼"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗌"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖮"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗋"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖼"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗁"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖺"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗋"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖽"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":["="]},{"tag":"mn","children":["0"]}]},"."]}]},{"tag":"h4","children":["Orchard Action verifying key selection"],"id":"orchardactionverifyingkeyselection"},{"tag":"p","children":["The correction to the Orchard Action circuit changes the Orchard Action verifying key after NU6.2 activation."]},{"tag":"p","children":["In § 4.1.13 ‘Zero-Knowledge Proving System’ ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["15"],"id":"fnref15","href":"#fn15"}]},", replace the sentence"]},{"tag":"blockquote","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["We also omit subscripts on ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖹"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖪"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖠"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖼"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mo","children":["."]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖯"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗋"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗏"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]}]}]}," and ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖹"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖪"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖠"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖼"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mo","children":["."]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖵"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗋"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖿"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗒"]}]}]},"."]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["with"]},{"tag":"blockquote","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["Subscripts are not omitted on ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖹"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖪"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖠"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖼"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mo","children":["."]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖯"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗋"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗏"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]}]}]}," and ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖹"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖪"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖠"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖼"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{