:"p","children":["Vulnerability disclosure: The pre-NU6.2 Orchard Action circuit had a soundness bug in its variable-base scalar multiplication gadget ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"id":"fnref6:1","href":"#fn6"}]},", which could have allowed balance violation. The bug is in the circuit implementation only; the Action statement specified above is as intended. The corrected circuit deployed at NU6.2 has a different verifying key, so pre-NU6.2 Action proofs verify only under the insecure pre-NU6.2 key, and NU6.2-onward proofs only under the corrected one. The two circuits differ only in the additional copy constraints added to ensure soundness ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["18"],"id":"fnref18","href":"#fn18"}]},". The consensus rule specifying which key is used for verification is in § 4.6 ‘Action Descriptions’."]}]},{"tag":"h4","children":["Canonical Orchard Action proof length"],"id":"canonicalorchardactionprooflength"},{"tag":"p","children":["Add a consensus rule in § 7.5 ‘Action Description Encoding and Consensus’"]},{"tag":"blockquote","children":[{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["[NU6.2 onward] The ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚙"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚛"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚘"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚘"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚏"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚜"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝙾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚛"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚌"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚑"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚊"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚛"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚍"]}]}]}," field MUST have the canonical length of ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mn","children":["2720"]},{"tag":"mo","children":["+"]},{"tag":"mn","children":["2272"]},{"tag":"mo","children":["⋅"]},{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚗"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝙰"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚌"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚝"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚒"]},{